<title>FRANCE: Infonie drops on 1996 loss.</title>
<headline>Infonie drops on 1996 loss.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in French online information company Infonie fell 8.76 percent to 125 francs on Wednesday after the company announced a 1996 loss of 149.2 million francs.</p>
<p>The company had said in February its loss would be more than 100 million.</p>
<p>Infonie, launched on the market in March 1996, has attracted 30,000 subscribers so far in the difficult Internet market in France.</p>
<p>Its low was 69 francs in December. The company is looking for an alliance with another service provider and aims to cut its break-even point.</p>
</text>
